INSERT INTO messages (id,conversation_id,role,content,created_at) VALUES ('3ac02110-221f-410a-a509-0f341da1bfd8','1401df1d-6271-4acd-8149-78f59375ae71','user','If referrals keep growing at the current rate, which hospital hits theatre or bed capacity first over the next quarter, how many more staff would we need, and what happens to waiting times?','2026-08-21 15:12:49.681556+00:00') ON CONFLICT (id) DO UPDATE SET conversation_id=EXCLUDED.conversation_id,role=EXCLUDED.role,content=EXCLUDED.content,created_at=EXCLUDED.created_at;
INSERT INTO messages (id,conversation_id,role,content,created_at) VALUES ('f2c11b9b-5a5b-463c-893d-3613cb806e88','1401df1d-6271-4acd-8149-78f59375ae71','assistant','Springfield Hospital will reach both theatre and bed capacity first, will need nine additional staff members, and its waiting time will extend beyond the current 22.3 weeks.  

- Average theatre utilisation: **88.7 %**  
- Average bed occupancy: **88.2 %**  
- Current average waiting time: **22.3 weeks**  

**Additional staff required at Springfield Hospital (for a +7.5 % quarterly demand increase)**  

| Grade | Current | Additional | New total |
|---|---|---|---|
| HCA | 29 | +3 | 32 |
| ODP | 11 | +1 | 12 |
| RN | 37 | +3 | 40 |
| HOC | 4 | +1 | 5 |
| A&C | 12 | +1 | 13 |
| **Total** | **93** | **+9** | **102** |

*Waiting times are projected to rise as capacity is breached, likely adding several weeks to the existing 22.3‑week average.*

_Sources: Capacity, Bed occupancy, Waiting time, Workforce, Staff delta_','2026-08-21 15:13:21.418855+00:00') ON CONFLICT (id) DO UPDATE SET conversation_id=EXCLUDED.conversation_id,role=EXCLUDED.role,content=EXCLUDED.content,created_at=EXCLUDED.created_at;
INSERT INTO messages (id,conversation_id,role,content,created_at) VALUES ('193a9e39-6573-468b-90b6-d3157302a257','4ac6f6f6-027c-4ff6-b8c3-b554965ab36b','user','If I close 2 theatres for 3 days at Springfield Hospital from 2026-09-14 to 2026-09-16, what are the implications? Which surgeries are impacted and can they be shifted elsewhere? What is the earliest date to do this with least disruption?','2026-08-21 15:13:29.077045+00:00') ON CONFLICT (id) DO UPDATE SET conversation_id=EXCLUDED.conversation_id,role=EXCLUDED.role,content=EXCLUDED.content,created_at=EXCLUDED.created_at;
INSERT INTO messages (id,conversation_id,role,content,created_at) VALUES ('a3f4c040-ea90-418a-9d22-90d32b2f83e5','62d2340f-be8a-4d12-a2a6-4655950359a9','assistant','Springfield Hospital has higher theatre utilisation (88.7 %) and a longer average wait (22.3 wk) than Ashtead Hospital (84.1 % utilisation, 19.6 wk).  

- Springfield Hospital – utilisation 88.7 %; wait 22.3 wk  
- Ashtead Hospital – utilisation 84.1 %; wait 19.6 wk  

*Sources: Capacity, Throughput & Flow*','2026-08-25 02:28:40.973057+00:00') ON CONFLICT (id) DO UPDATE SET conversation_id=EXCLUDED.conversation_id,role=EXCLUDED.role,content=EXCLUDED.content,created_at=EXCLUDED.created_at;
INSERT INTO messages (id,conversation_id,role,content,created_at) VALUES ('ae7ccef9-e678-40a5-99c1-ccbb0e2be6aa','4ac6f6f6-027c-4ff6-b8c3-b554965ab36b','assistant','Closing two theatres at Springfield Hospital for three days (14‑16 Sep 2026) will affect roughly 53 scheduled cases; these can be re‑allocated to other sites using their available three‑day slack, leaving one case (≈55 minutes) to be deferred to a later date.  

**Impacted surgeries (estimated cases)**  

- Ophthalmology: 10 cases  
- Medical Oncology: 10 cases  
- Gastroenterology: 8 cases  
- Gynaecology: 7 cases  
- ENT: 5 cases  
- Pain Management: 3 cases  
- Urology: 3 cases  
- General Surgery: 3 cases  
- Trauma & Orthopaedics: 2 cases  

**Re‑allocation to receiving sites (using network slack)**  

| From site / specialty | Cases | To site | Utilisation after shift |
|-----------------------|-------|---------|--------------------------|
| Springfield (all) | 14 | Rivers Hospital | 88.7 % → 93.0 % |
| Springfield (all) | 17 | Oaklands Hospital | 65.8 % → 71.0 % |
| Springfield (all) | 13 | Pinehill Hospital | 76.2 % → 81.0 % |
| Springfield (all) | 9 | Ashtead Hospital | 84.1 % → 89.0 % |
| – | 1 (≈55 min) | – | Deferred to next available slot at Springfield (post‑16 Sep) |

**Earliest low‑disruption window**  
The proposed dates (14‑16 Sep 2026) already align with the maximum available slack across the network; only a single case must be postponed. No earlier period offers greater spare capacity, so the earliest date with least disruption is the requested window, with the residual case deferred to the first open slot after 16 Sep 2026.  

*Sources: Capacity, Throughput & Flow, Patient Activity & Finance*','2026-08-21 15:13:59.338600+00:00') ON CONFLICT (id) DO UPDATE SET conversation_id=EXCLUDED.conversation_id,role=EXCLUDED.role,content=EXCLUDED.content,created_at=EXCLUDED.created_at;
INSERT INTO messages (id,conversation_id,role,content,created_at) VALUES ('f0f2310d-b46e-4529-acf9-eecd7943c40d','3b779abd-0614-408d-bc0e-5c9aeabcfc22','user','If I close 2 theatres for 3 days at Springfield Hospital from 2026-09-14 to 2026-09-16, what are the implications? Which surgeries are impacted and can they be shifted elsewhere? What is the earliest date to do this with least disruption?','2026-08-23 07:27:59.277086+00:00') ON CONFLICT (id) DO UPDATE SET conversation_id=EXCLUDED.conversation_id,role=EXCLUDED.role,content=EXCLUDED.content,created_at=EXCLUDED.created_at;
INSERT INTO messages (id,conversation_id,role,content,created_at) VALUES ('84d367d5-e4f0-48d3-a6ce-510979864da1','3b779abd-0614-408d-bc0e-5c9aeabcfc22','assistant','Closing two theatres at Springfield Hospital for three days (2026‑09‑14 to 2026‑09‑16) will affect approximately **51 scheduled cases**; 47 of these can be re‑allocated to other sites without exceeding their available slack, leaving **4 cases** that must be deferred at Springfield.

- Total cases scheduled at Springfield over the next 30 days: 1,272 → ≈ 42 cases per day.  
- Capacity loss from closing two of an assumed five theatres: 40 % → ≈ 17 cases per day × 3 days = **51 cases** impacted.  
- Network spare capacity (3‑day slack) across receiving sites: 2,825 minutes → enough for **≈ 47 cases** (assuming 60 minutes per case).  

**Shift plan (minutes → cases, rounded):**

| From site / specialty | Cases affected | To site | Slack minutes used | Cases re‑allocated |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Springfield – all specialties | 51 | Oaklands Hospital | 909 | 15 |
| Springfield – all specialties | 51 | Rivers Hospital | 752 | 12 |
| Springfield – all specialties | 51 | Pinehill Hospital | 685 | 11 |
| Springfield – all specialties | 51 | Ashtead Hospital | 479 | 7 |
| **Total re‑allocated** | 51 | **–** | **2,825** | **45** |
| **Remaining at Springfield** | 51 | – | – | **4** (deferred) |

The earliest date that minimises disruption is the proposed window (14‑16 September 2026); it utilises the full network slack and leaves only a small residual backlog of four cases, which can be scheduled immediately after theatres reopen. Any later closure would not increase available slack and would therefore not reduce disruption further.

*Sources: Capacity, Throughput & Flow, Deterministic Guardrail*','2026-08-23 07:28:05.379022+00:00') ON CONFLICT (id) DO UPDATE SET conversation_id=EXCLUDED.conversation_id,role=EXCLUDED.role,content=EXCLUDED.content,created_at=EXCLUDED.created_at;
INSERT INTO messages (id,conversation_id,role,content,created_at) VALUES ('6ee6ebb7-1fb3-478d-a66f-d23c33ecfa98','e906eca4-f80c-4f09-91c2-dc8d35251e40','user','If referrals keep growing at the current rate, which hospital hits theatre or bed capacity first over the next quarter, how many more staff would we need, and what happens to waiting times?','2026-08-23 07:29:01.112730+00:00') ON CONFLICT (id) DO UPDATE SET conversation_id=EXCLUDED.conversation_id,role=EXCLUDED.role,content=EXCLUDED.content,created_at=EXCLUDED.created_at;
INSERT INTO messages (id,conversation_id,role,content,created_at) VALUES ('e7bcf586-d4d0-4a51-8fab-dc97197ff780','e906eca4-f80c-4f09-91c2-dc8d35251e40','assistant','Springfield Hospital will reach theatre and bed capacity first if referrals continue to grow at the current rate.  

- **Capacity breach:** Springfield’s average theatre utilisation (88.7 %) and bed occupancy (88.2 %) are the highest, leaving the smallest margin before 100 % capacity.  
- **Additional staff required at Springfield:**  

| Grade | Current | Additional | New total |
|---|---|---|---|
| HCA | 29 | +3 | 32 |
| ODP | 11 | +1 | 12 |
| RN | 37 | +3 | 40 |
| HOC | 4 | +1 | 5 |
| A&C | 12 | +1 | 13 |
| **Total** | **93** | **+9** | **102** |

- **Waiting‑time impact:** With utilisation rising from 88.7 % to 100 %, waiting time at Springfield is projected to increase proportionally from 22.3 weeks to roughly 25 weeks (an additional ≈ 2.9 weeks). Other sites will see smaller rises, remaining below 20 weeks.

*Sources: Capacity, Workforce*','2026-08-23 07:29:08.204072+00:00') ON CONFLICT (id) DO UPDATE SET conversation_id=EXCLUDED.conversation_id,role=EXCLUDED.role,content=EXCLUDED.content,created_at=EXCLUDED.created_at;
