e ones with the highest wait times and tell me the root cause.", "per_agent": [{"sql": "SELECT `SiteName`, AVG(`WeeksWaiting`) AS avg_waiting_weeks, try_divide(100.0 * SUM(`RTTBreach`),COUNT(*)) AS rtt_breach_pct FROM `ramsay_health`.`ops`.`vw_waiting_list` WHERE `SiteName` IS NOT NULL AND `WeeksWaiting` IS NOT NULL GROUP BY `SiteName`", "agent": "throughput_flow", "error": null, "row_count": 5, "agentLabel": "Throughput & Flow", "latency_ms": 12872, "row_preview": [["Ashtead Hospital", "19.549342105263158", "31.68859649122807"], ["Pinehill Hospital", "16.294954721862872", "19.87925830099181"], ["Oaklands Hospital", "12.511417950079661", "9.55921402018056"], ["Springfield Hospital", "22.26191237607931", "40.42212983690438"], ["Rivers Hospital", "11.27390180878553", "7.95865633074935"]], "sub_question": "What are the average waiting time in weeks and RTT breach percentage by hospital?"}], "chart_spec": {"data": [{"avg_wait": 11.2739, "hospital": "Rivers Hospital"}, {"avg_wait": 22.2619, "hospital": "Springfield Hospital"}], "title": "Average Waiting Time by Hospital", "xField": "hospital", "yField": "avg_wait", "chartType": "bar"}, "agents_called": ["Throughput & Flow"], "guardrail_events": [], "agent_keys_called": ["throughput_flow"], "final_answer_text": "Rivers Hospital has the lowest average wait time (11.3\u202fweeks) and Springfield Hospital the highest (22.3\u202fweeks); the root cause for this disparity is not provided in the available data.\n\n- Rivers Hospital \u2013 11.3\u202fweeks average wait  \n- Springfield Hospital \u2013 22.3\u202fweeks average wait  \n\n*Sources: Throughput & Flow*"}}, {"stage": "done", "demoMode": false, "conversationId": "ce29e341-1eb3-4277-ad02-c8a7e38658e2"}]'::jsonb,'2026-08-21 15:12:12.498555+00:00') ON CONFLICT (id) DO UPDATE SET conversation_id=EXCLUDED.conversation_id,turn_id=EXCLUDED.turn_id,events=EXCLUDED.events,created_at=EXCLUDED.created_at;
INSERT INTO traces (id,conversation_id,turn_id,events,created_at) VALUES ('50be4455-a55d-4f7a-a7c1-14532aa6000f','55f6270f-34eb-4f5c-9a9c-c5b181fa66a8','af9034d2-ea54-41fe-9d3e-152dda90bd22','[{"stage": "decompose_start"}, {"stage": "decompose", "subquestions": ["How many patients over 55 referred for Trauma and Orthopaedics are on an admitted RTT pathway by hospital?"]}, {"stage": "route", "routes": [{"agent": "patient_finance", "question": "How many patients over 55 referred for Trauma and Orthopaedics are on an admitted RTT pathway by hospital?", "rationale": "Counts patients by age, specialty, RTT pathway status, and hospital", "agentLabel": "Patient Activity & Finance"}]}, {"count": 1, "stage": "agents_start"}, {"agent": "patient_finance", "stage": "agent_call_start", "question": "How many patients over 55 referred for Trauma and Orthopaedics are on an admitted RTT pathway by hospital?", "agentLabel": "Patient Activity & Finance"}, {"sql": "SELECT w.LocationName AS Hospital, COUNT(*) AS Patients\nFROM ramsay_health.ops.tbreferrals r\nJOIN ramsay_health.ops.tbwlmds w ON r.ReferralID = w.ReferralID\nWHERE r.AgeAtDateOfReferral > 55 AND r.ServiceName = ''Trauma and Orthopaedics'' AND r.HasAdmission = 1 AND w.LocationName IS NOT NULL\nGROUP BY w.LocationName\nORDER BY Patients DESC", "rows": [["Springfield Hospital", "288"], ["Ashtead Hospital", "226"], ["Pinehill Hospital", "216"], ["Rivers Hospital", "190"], ["Oaklands Hospital", "179"]], "agent": "patient_finance", "error": null, "stage": "agent_call_done", "answer": "The number of patients over 55 referred for Trauma and Orthopaedics and admitted on an RTT pathway varies by hospital. Notable data points include:\n- **Springfield Hospital:** 288 patients\n- **Ashtead Hospital:** 226 patients\n- **Pinehill Hospital:** 216 patients\n- **Rivers Hospital:** 190 patients\n- **Oaklands Hospital:** 179 patients\nSpringfield Hospital has the highest number of such patients among the hospitals listed.", "columns": ["Hosp